Hi,

Attached is the relicensing research memo requested, in both editable (.docx)=
 and presentation-ready (.pdf) form.

It covers all four angles:
  1. Legal foundations =E2=80=94 why relicensing is a copyright question (own=
ership, CLA vs DCO, irrevocable prior releases, direction-of-travel).
  2. Process =E2=80=94 a 7-step how-to for relicensing a project we own, with=
 a "who do I need to ask?" decision tree.
  3. Feasibility & risk =E2=80=94 a 6-factor scoring matrix (0-18) that grade=
s any proposed change Trivial / Moderate / Hard / Impractical, plus a "when t=
o pay a lawyer" section.
  4. Third-party impact =E2=80=94 what to do when a dependency relicenses on =
us (the MongoDB -> Elastic -> HashiCorp -> Redis pattern), sized by how we us=
e it.

Appendices include copy-paste contributor-consent templates, a license-compat=
ibility quick reference, and a glossary. Precedents/dates verified against ve=
ndor announcements and OSI records.

Two placeholders still need filling before this goes further: the "Prepared f=
or" and "Prepared by" names on the cover. Flag me the names and I'll finalize.

Note: this is general information for internal planning, not legal advice.

Best,
Hermes

